re, the first drop at mid pic, and the bottom of el horrendo is visible further upstream","caption":"Afterbirth","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14282","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14282"}},{"id":"14277","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"This one is sick.  A class 3 technical jaunt piles right into a sieve on the right.  its hard to avoid and you would probably die if you went in there.  This is the fourth and final drop of the first gorge.","caption":"Baby Jesus","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14277","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14277"}},{"id":"14276","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"This is the third drop in the first gorge.  I know it looks tight, but trust me, its even tighter.  ","caption":"fantasy flight","poi_name":"","subject":"Tony Robinson","author":"KE","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14276","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14276"}},{"id":"14288","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"This is in the middle of fat man's.  Yes, a kayak will fit, but not all the way under and out.","caption":"Now THAT\"S a sieve","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14288","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14288"}},{"id":"892294","ext":"jpg","post_id":"896194","description":null,"caption":"Obey, E. Fork @Cliff Springs to TN 85 Bridge","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/892294","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/892294"}},{"id":"892295","ext":"jpg","post_id":"896195","description":null,"caption":"Snowing from Putin to take out","poi_name":"Put in","subject":null,"author":"Dave Fulcher","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/892295","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/892295"}},{"id":"14284","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"Drive right and plane the hole heading right.  Probably won't kill you, but scary none the less.  Its a deep undercut on the left, where the rebound off the right wall all goes.  Speed will prevent you from going there as well","caption":"Close up of second drop of afterbirth","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14284","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14284"}},{"id":"108","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2530","description":"See more of Julie Keller's photos at (<a href=\"http://www.juliekeller.com/\">www.JulieKeller.com</a>). ","caption":"East Fork Obey","poi_name":"","subject":"Fran Fitzpatrick","author":"Julie Keller (www.JulieKeller.com)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/108","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/108"}},{"id":"14286","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"","caption":"Alex Zendel keeping the bow up","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14286","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14286"}},{"id":"14311","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4593","description":"Tom dropping into the first gorge on river right.","caption":"First gorge, top drop","poi_name":"First gorge, top drop","subject":"Tom Zimmerman","author":"Trent Pearce","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14311","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14311"}},{"id":"14285","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"Don't get me wrong, we had moments of fun between the boring parts","caption":"Scenery and whitewater","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14285","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14285"}},{"id":"14287","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"","caption":"Tony scouting Fat Man's Squeeze","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14287","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14287"}},{"id":"14289","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"","caption":"Looking downstream from Fat Man's Squeeze","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14289","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14289"}},{"id":"14279","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"See that flat rock on the right?  If you go under there its over.  Stay left","caption":"Looking into el horrendo","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14279","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14279"}},{"id":"14280","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"Look at this one real carefully.  Any mistake could be fatal.  anywhere off line is bad.  There are 3 undercuts and countless sieves in here.  there is a siphon on river right on the bottom drop.","caption":"El horrendo from the bottom","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"KE","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14280","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14280"}},{"id":"14274","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"This is where you get out and scout the first of 4 drops, which mostly comprise one single large class 5.  This spot is the prettiest on the river.","caption":"Top of first gorge","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Kirk Eddlemon","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14274","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14274"}},{"id":"14275","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"This is the second drop in the first gorge.","caption":"a fun slot","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14275","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14275"}},{"id":"14278","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"This is the top of el horrendo","caption":"Getting out to scout gorge #2","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14278","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14278"}},{"id":"14283","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"Tony is droping the first drop of afterbirth","caption":"Tony on afterbirth","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14283","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14283"}},{"id":"14281","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5470","description":"This is the first drop of afterbirth, which is right below el horrendo.  There is a hole and hallway visible in the picture.  The top is tricky and then around the corner to the right, it immediately drops into a slot that would not be runnable if it was 2 inches tighter.  It is very undercut.","caption":"looking down the gut at Afterbirth","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14281","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14281"}}],"detail":{"id":"1777","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"_Photo of Fran Fitzpatrick, courtesy of Julie Keller ( [www.JulieKeller.com](http://www.juliekeller.com))._\n\n_Canoeing and Kayaking Guide to the Streams of Tennessee_, B. Sehlinger and\n\nThis is a strange run, with lots of flatwater punctuated by extremely dangerous rapids. Many paddlers had fun on this run--and said they wouldn't be back. See the Comments tab for their testimony.","averageGradient":"40","maxGradient":"130","length":"13.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"1777","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"1000","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"EAST FORK OBEY RIVER NEAR JAMESTOWN, TN","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"03414500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ARCHIVED","latestFlowReading":{"value":"12.7","dateTime":"2019-10-01T05:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":null,"location":{"latitude":"36.41617895","longitude":"-85.02634019"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/03414500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"ht